### Frontend Rules (Repo: flowtron)

Stack: Vite + React + TypeScript + Tailwind + Zustand + Vitest

General

- Keep components small, focused, and accessible (ARIA, keyboard navigation, focus states, color contrast)
- Prefer composition over inheritance; lift state only when necessary
- Avoid premature abstractions; extract utilities only with clear reuse

TypeScript

- Explicit types for exported APIs; avoid `any` and unsafe casts
- Use discriminated unions for variant state; prefer `unknown` over `any`
- Model complex conditions with well-named booleans/derived selectors

React

- Functional components only; follow Rules of Hooks
- Memoization: use `useMemo`/`useCallback` narrowly for measurable wins
- State: colocate; prefer local state; use Zustand for cross-cutting app state
- Effects: side effects belong in `useEffect`; avoid effects for pure derivations

Styling (Tailwind)

- Utility-first; keep class lists readable and consistent
- Extract reusable patterns into components or Tailwind presets when repeated
- Respect dark mode and responsive variants as needed

Data & Store (Zustand)

- Keep store minimal and serializable; derive computed selectors instead of duplicating
- Avoid storing transient UI state globally unless necessary

Testing (Vitest + React Testing Library if added)

- Write tests for critical paths and regressions
- Prefer behavior-oriented tests over implementation details

Quality & CI

- Run `npm run lint` and `npm run test` locally before marking tasks complete
- Fix lints rather than disabling rules, unless there is a justified exception

Performance & Accessibility

- Measure before optimizing; avoid premature micro-optimizations
- Include basic a11y checks; ensure interactive elements are reachable by keyboard

File & Naming Conventions

- Components in `PascalCase.tsx`; hooks in `use*.ts`
- Descriptive names; avoid abbreviations that reduce clarity

Operational Notes

- Use status updates before running tools; parallelize read-only discovery
- Keep edits minimal and scoped; avoid reformatting unrelated files

